  "id": "reflex-arc",
  "term": "reflex arc",
  "definition": "A reflex arc is a feedback pathway in which stretch sensed by a muscle spindle is sent through a sensory neuron to spinal cord motor neurons, which then trigger the muscle to contract. In this example, the response opposes further stretching and helps maintain normal muscle tone.",
